@title MotorStorm RC - reach the main-screen sandbox
@game  PCSA00027
@shot-every 60   # in-game shots through the boot so a human can judge render quality

# ============================================================================
# GOAL
# Reach the MAIN SCREEN: a top-down RC car sandbox in a skatepark, which is a
# live 3D scene and therefore the render-quality proving ground.
#
# THE ONE GATE BEFORE THE MAIN SCREEN
# A save-less first boot lands on an ONLINE TERMS (EULA) accept/decline screen
# and waits there forever with no input. Cross = ACCEPT. On real hardware you
# accept once and it is saved, so later boots skip straight to the sandbox; we
# have no saved acceptance, so this recipe scripts the accept every run.
#
# FRAME NUMBERS ARE POST-2026-07-25. Before that date a plain cooperative yield
# (sceKernelDelayThread(0), sceDisplayWaitVblankStartMulti(0)) was counted as a
# display frame, so this title's frame clock ran roughly 80x fast while a worker
# spun. Every landmark below was re-measured against the corrected clock, where
# one frame is one sceGxmDisplayQueueAddEntry. Old recipes' frame numbers are
# meaningless; do not port them.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
# (no input) - legal splash to ~f450, then a "Communicating with server" spinner
# (~f600), then the ONLINE TERMS panel fades in and is live and scrolling by f800.

# --- accept the terms with a single brief Cross press ---
820: @section accept-terms
820: cross          # ACCEPT. Held 12 frames: the guest samples the pad once per
832:                 # display frame, so a press must span several frames to be seen.

# --- the sandbox loads in behind a tutorial dialog ---
850: @section post-accept
900:  @shot post-accept-0900
1000: @shot post-accept-1000
1100: @shot post-accept-1100
1200: @shot main-screen-1200   # sandbox fully up: skatepark, both RC cars, the
                               # "Welcome to the MotorStorm RC tutorial" dialog.
1200: @note This recipe stops at the main screen on purpose - it is the render target.
1200: @note To play the tutorial, use tutorial-drive.recipe, which continues from here.
